Subject: Relax and restore PDBs the way the API server accepts

Why: the runbook template relaxes a blocking PDB by merging maxUnavailable into it, which the API server rejects on a PDB that sets minAvailable, and restores it by re-applying a dump the API server answers with a 409 conflict. The patch clears minAvailable in the relax step, restores the PDB as a numbered, verified step, and aligns SKILL.md's rule and troubleshooting.md §1 with it.
Local-Issue: none (#2353)
Upstream-Issue: none filed yet
Retire-When: upstream's runbook relaxes and restores PDBs the way the API server accepts

